  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The phone's two ways in",
      "items": [
        "USB: scripts/usb.sh runs adb reverse, so the phone opens http://localhost:8790, a secure page for the camera without a certificate (usb.sh 10–17).",
        "Wi-Fi: ./start.sh --make-cert gives the edge its own authority; the setup page shows a QR code for it and one for the page, and the phone installs the authority once (setup.js 116–118, make_cert.sh 5–13).",
        "/ws refuses a foreign Origin and a wrong key; a new phone takes over and the old one is closed with 4000 (wsserver.py 368–373, 265–269)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "One contract, three transports",
      "items": [
        "The core hands every event to each adapter that is on and takes commands from any (core.py 69–86, 155–191); --adapter picks them (adapters/__init__.py 49–60).",
        "nodered: /ws/backend on the edge's own port, with the token from .edge/token; without a token only this PC (wsserver.py 359–367).",
        "mqtt: dhc/edge/<id>/event/<t>, /command, a retained /status with an offline last will (mqtt.py 39–40, 61–86). ros2: two std_msgs/String topics with the same JSON (ros2.py 36–64)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Kept on the edge, and not",
      "items": [
        "The edge keeps the profile shown, the tiles' states and labels, the last 60 events and the photos of the last 6, in memory only (core.py 28–29, 69–80).",
        "Nothing is written but the phone checks' reports (registry); records go to the backend, which owns them (examples/inventory.json 70–71)."
      ]
    }
  ]
